    <string name="label_camera">Camera</string>
    <string name="camera_detection_title">Camera detection</string>
    <string name="camera_only_label">Only while a camera app is running</string>
    <string name="camera_only_description">Uses the camera becoming unavailable as the signal that another app has it open. This app never opens a camera itself.</string>
    <string name="camera_not_reported">Camera availability is not being reported on this device.</string>
    <string name="camera_none_held">No camera app is holding the camera right now.</string>
    <string name="camera_held_by_other">%1$d of %2$d cameras held by another app: %3$s</string>
    <string name="camera_unavailable_warning">This device does not report camera availability, so with the option on the mappings would never run.</string>
    <string name="recording_title">Recording</string>
    <string name="flip_restart_label">Restart video when the gimbal flips the phone</string>
    <string name="flip_restart_description">The camera being open does not mean it is recording, so this also checks whether the microphone is in use. When the gimbal swings the phone about 120 degrees or more while recording, the shutter is pressed to end the clip and pressed again shortly after to start a new one the right way up. Off by default, because it takes control of the camera app.</string>
    <string name="label_microphone">Microphone</string>
    <string name="label_recording_video">Recording video</string>
    <string name="recording_no_camera_only">no, only the camera is in use</string>
    <string name="microphone_unavailable_warning">This device does not let other apps see whether the microphone is in use, so a video cannot be told apart from a photo and the flip restart will not trigger. Everything else is unaffected.</string>
    <string name="shutter_title">On-screen shutter</string>
    <string name="shutter_description">When a trigger is mapped to \"Press on-screen shutter\", three routes are tried: a button that names itself as a shutter, then the pixels of a screenshot, then a button that merely sits and is shaped where a shutter usually is. Colour is only a tie-breaker, because an accessibility tree carries no pixels and not every shutter is white or red.</string>
    <string name="shutter_no_attempt">No attempt yet. Trigger it from a camera app, then come back here — the result cannot be shown while another app is in front.</string>
